      "content": "Considering your symptoms, it's possible that you may be experiencing effects from the long flight due to dehydration, jet lag, and changes in air pressure. However, the sore and swollen calf could also be a real injury, such as a deep vein thrombosis (DVT) or blood clot, which are not uncommon with long-distance travel. Since you're concerned, it's always best to err on the side of caution and consult with a doctor to rule out any underlying conditions. Seeing a doctor quickly will help alleviate your concerns and provide a proper diagnosis and treatment plan.",
